Chr3	Araport11	gene	619678	623739	.	-	.	ID=AT3G02850;Name=AT3G02850;Note=STELAR K+ outward rectifier;curator_summary=Encodes SKOR%2C a member of Shaker family potassium ion (K+) channel.  This family includes five groups based on phylogenetic analysis (FEBS Letters (2007) 581: 2357): I (inward rectifying channel): AKT1 (AT2G26650)%2C AKT5 (AT4G32500) and SPIK (also known as AKT6%2C AT2G25600)%3B II (inward rectifying channel): KAT1 (AT5G46240) and KAT2 (AT4G18290)%3B III (weakly inward rectifying channel): AKT2 (AT4G22200)%3B IV (regulatory subunit involved in inwardly rectifying conductance formation): KAT3 (also known as AtKC1%2C AT4G32650)%3B V (outward rectifying channel): SKOR (AT3G02850) and GORK (AT5G37500).  Mediates the delivery of K+ from stelar cells to the xylem in the roots towards the shoot. mRNA accumulation is modulated by abscisic acid. K+ gating activity is modulated by external and internal K+.;symbol=SKOR;full_name=STELAR K+ outward rectifier;computational_description=STELAR K+ outward rectifier (SKOR)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: outward rectifier potassium channel activity%2C cyclic nucleotide binding%3B INVOLVED IN: potassium ion transport%2C response to abscisic acid stimulus%3B LOCATED IN: membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 8 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: L mature pollen stage%2C M germinated pollen stage%2C 4 anthesis%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Cyclic nucleotide-binding (InterPro:IPR000595)%2C Potassium channel%2C voltage-dependent%2C EAG/ELK/ERG (InterPro:IPR003938)%2C Protein of unknown function DUF3354 (InterPro:IPR021789)%2C Ankyrin repeat-containing domain (InterPro:IPR020683)%2C Ion transport (InterPro:IPR005821)%2C Cyclic nucleotide-binding-like (InterPro:IPR018490)%2C RmlC-like jelly roll fold (InterPro:IPR014710)%2C Ankyrin repeat (InterPro:IPR002110)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: gated outwardly-rectifying K+ channel (TAIR:AT5G37500.1)%3B Has 82938 Blast hits to 34972 proteins in 1815 species: Archae - 147%3B Bacteria - 10