Chr3	Araport11	gene	1603359	1606243	.	+	.	ID=AT3G05530;Name=AT3G05530;Note=regulatory particle triple-A ATPase 5A;curator_summary=Encodes RPT5a (Regulatory Particle 5a)%2C one of the six AAA-ATPases of the proteasome regulatory particle.  Essential for gametophyte development.  In Arabidopsis%2C the RPT5 subunit is encoded by two highly homologous genes%2C RPT5a and RPT5b.  RPT5a and RPT5b show accession-dependent functional redundancy.  In Wassilewskija (Ws) accession: mutant alleles of RPT5a displayed 50%25 pollen lethality%2C indicating that RPT5a is essential for male gametophyte development. In the Columbia (Col) accession%2C a rpt5a mutant allele did not display such a phenotype because the RPT5b Col allele complements the rpt5a defect in the male gametophyte%2C whereas the RPT5b Ws allele does not. Double rpt5a rpt5b mutants in Col background showed a complete male and female gametophyte lethal phenotype.;symbol=RPT5A;Alias=ATS6A.2;full_name=regulatory particle triple-A ATPase 5A;computational_description=regulatory particle triple-A ATPase 5A (RPT5A)%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: ATPase%2C AAA+ type%2C core (InterPro:IPR003593)%2C ATPase%2C AAA-type%2C core (InterPro:IPR003959)%2C ATPase%2C AAA-type%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR003960)%2C 26S proteasome subunit P45 (InterPro:IPR005937)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: 26S proteasome AAA-ATPase subunit RPT5B (TAIR:AT1G09100.1)%3B Has 33265 Blast hits to 30927 proteins in 3145 species: Archae - 1437%3B Bacteria - 12044%3B Metazoa - 4947%3B Fungi - 3672%3B Plants - 3322%3B Viruses - 56%3B Other Eukaryotes - 7787 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:10417703,PMID:10363660,PMID:11782485,PMID:11742986,PMID:11179422,PMID:9741626,PMID:12692151,PMID:15610358,PMID:17028202,PMID:17307927,PMID:18650403,PMID:18775970,PMID:19223514,PMID:20516081,PMID:20682047,PMID:21389614,PMID:21784786,PMID:24846764,locus:2079742;locus_type=protein_coding
