Chr3	Araport11	gene	2255710	2258204	.	-	.	ID=AT3G07130;Name=AT3G07130;Note=purple acid phosphatase 15;curator_summary=Encodes PAP15%2C a purple acid phosphatase with phytase activity.  Expression of PAP15 is developmentally and temporally regulated%2C with strong expression at the early stages of seedling growth and pollen germination. The expression is also organ/tissue-specific%2C with strongest expression in the vasculature%2C pollen grains%2C and roots. Recombinant PAP protein exhibits broad substrate specificity with moderate phytase activity. PAP15 likely mobilizes phosphorus reserves in plants%2C particularly during seed and pollen germination.;symbol=PAP15;Alias=ATPAP15,PURPLE ACID PHOSPHATASE 15;full_name=purple acid phosphatase 15;computational_description=purple acid phosphatase 15 (PAP15)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: protein serine/threonine phosphatase activity%2C acid phosphatase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: pollen germination%2C seed germination%3B LOCATED IN: endomembrane system%3B EXPRESSED IN: 11 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: seedling growth%2C petal differentiation and expansion stage%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Purple acid phosphatase%2C N-terminal (InterPro:IPR015914)%2C Metallophosphoesterase (InterPro:IPR004843)%2C Purple acid phosphatase-like%2C N-terminal (InterPro:IPR008963)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: purple acid phosphatase 13 (TAIR:AT2G32770.3)%3B Has 2322 Blast hits to 2305 proteins in 472 species: Archae - 7%3B Bacteria - 914%3B Metazoa - 228%3B Fungi - 75%3B Plants - 768%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 330 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12021284,PMID:16244908,PMID:18796151,PMID:19587103,PMID:19633233,PMID:20736450,PMID:25048220,locus:2098500;locus_type=protein_coding
