Chr3	Araport11	gene	2264862	2279916	.	-	.	ID=AT3G07160;Name=AT3G07160;Note=glucan synthase-like 10;curator_summary=Encodes GSL10%2C a member of the Glucan Synthase-Like (GSL) family believed to be involved in the synthesis of the cell wall component callose.  GSL10 is required for male gametophyte development and plant growth.  Has a role in entry of microspores into mitosis.  GSL10 mutation leads to perturbation of microspore division symmetry%2C irregular callose deposition and failure of generative cell engulfment by the vegetative cell cytoplasm.  Also refer to GSL8 (At2g36850).;symbol=GSL10;Alias=ATGSL10,glucan synthase-like 10,CALS9,gsl10;full_name=glucan synthase-like 10;computational_description=glucan synthase-like 10 (GSL10)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: 1%2C3-beta-glucan synthase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: in 8 processes%3B LOCATED IN: 1%2C3-beta-glucan synthase complex%2C plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 25 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 14 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Glycosyl transferase%2C family 48 (InterPro:IPR003440)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: glucan synthase-like 8 (TAIR:AT2G36850.1)%3B Has 1244 Blast hits to 899 proteins in 149 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 5%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 674%3B Plants - 491%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 74 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:15235117,PMID:16618929,PMID:16615871,PMID:17660356,PMID:18315544,PMID:18760496,PMID:18775970,PMID:20039178,PMID:21451254,PMID:21116665,locus:2098565;locus_type=protein_coding
