Chr3	Araport11	gene	2425884	2433113	.	+	.	ID=AT3G07610;Name=AT3G07610;Note=Transcription factor jumonji (jmjC) domain-containing protein;curator_summary=IBM1 likely encodes a protein with histone H3mK9 demethylation activity. It may preferentially demethylate H3mK9 at low-copy loci to protect them from silencing by nearby heterochromatin by preventing the spread of cytosine methylation. BONSAI (At1g73177) is hypermethylated in ibm1 mutants. ibm1 mutants have morphological defects that become apparent at the F3 generation%2C including small narrow leaves%2C arrested flower development%2C and faulty pollen development. These phenotypes cannot result solely from the BONSAI hypermethylation. Aberrant phenotypes in ibm1 mutants in both DNA methylation and plant development can be suppressed by mutations in the KYP H3K9 methyltransferase or he CMT3 non CG-cytosine methylase.;symbol=IBM1;full_name=increase in bonsai methylation 1;computational_description=increase in bonsai methylation 1 (IBM1)%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Transcription factor jumonji/aspartyl beta-hydroxylase (InterPro:IPR003347)%2C Transcription factor jumonji (InterPro:IPR013129)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Transcription factor jumonji (jmjC) domain-containing protein (TAIR:AT1G11950.1)%3B Has 4122 Blast hits to 1300 proteins in 255 species: Archae - 5%3B Bacteria - 1758%3B Metazoa - 460%3B Fungi - 93%3B Plants - 912%3B Viruses - 8%3B Other Eukaryotes - 886 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:11983057,PMID:18218897,PMID:19262562,PMID:18567943,PMID:20834229,PMID:22580822,PMID:22772985,PMID:23313553,PMID:23934508,PMID:24003136,PMID:24404182,PMID:24248388,PMID:24204292,locus:2091117;locus_type=protein_coding
