Chr3	Araport11	gene	3346509	3351170	.	-	.	ID=AT3G10700;Name=AT3G10700;Note=galacturonic acid kinase;curator_summary=Encodes a GHMP kinase family protein that acts as a galacturonic acid-1-phosphate kinase that catalyzes the production of galacturonic acid-1-phosphate. This is a precursor of the important cell wall building block UDP-galacturonic acid.  Based on gene trap line GT8007%2C the gene appears to be expressed in a petal and stamen-specific manner%2C between flower stages 8 to 11%2C however%2C later RT-qPCR analysis demonstrates that the transcript is present throughout the plant in all tissues tested.;symbol=GalAK;full_name=galacturonic acid kinase;computational_description=galacturonic acid kinase (GalAK)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: ATP binding%2C galactokinase activity%2C galacturonokinase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: carbohydrate phosphorylation%2C D-galacturonate metabolic process%3B LOCATED IN: cytoplasm%3B EXPRESSED IN: 21 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Galactokinase (InterPro:IPR000705)%2C Mevalonate/galactokinase (InterPro:IPR006206)%2C Ribosomal protein S5 domain 2-type fold (InterPro:IPR020568)%2C GHMP kinase (InterPro:IPR006204)%2C Ribosomal protein S5 domain 2-type fold%2C subgroup (InterPro:IPR014721)%2C GHMP kinase%2C C-terminal (InterPro:IPR013750)%3B Has 3493 Blast hits to 3446 proteins in 1360 species: Archae - 42%3B Bacteria - 2414%3B Metazoa - 241%3B Fungi - 181%3B Plants - 121%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 494 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:16055634,PMID:17597079,PMID:19509290,locus:2075730;locus_type=protein_coding
Chr3	Araport11	mRNA	3346509	3351170	.	-	.	ID=AT3G10700.1;Parent=AT3G10700;Name=AT3G10700.1;Note=galacturonic acid kinase;curator_summary=Encodes a GHMP kinase family protein that acts as a galacturonic acid-1-phosphate kinase that catalyzes the production of galacturonic acid-1-phosphate. This is a precursor of the important cell wall building block UDP-galacturonic acid.  Based on gene trap line GT8007%2C the gene appears to be expressed in a petal and stamen-specific manner%2C between flower stages 8 to 11%2C however%2C later RT-qPCR analysis demonstrates that the transcript is present throughout the plant in all tissues tested.;conf_class=1;symbol=GalAK;full_name=galacturonic acid kinase;computational_description=galacturonic acid kinase (GalAK)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: ATP binding%2C galactokinase activity%2C galacturonokinase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: carbohydrate phosphorylation%2C D-galacturonate metabolic process%3B LOCATED IN: cytoplasm%3B EXPRESSED IN: 21 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Galactokinase (InterPro:IPR000705)%2C Mevalonate/galactokinase (InterPro:IPR006206)%2C Ribosomal protein S5 domain 2-type fold (InterPro:IPR020568)%2C GHMP kinase (InterPro:IPR006204)%2C Ribosomal protein S5 domain 2-type fold%2C subgroup (InterPro:IPR014721)%2C GHMP kinase%2C C-terminal (InterPro:IPR013750)%3B Has 3493 Blast hits to 3446 proteins in 1360 species: Archae - 42%3B Bacteria - 2414%3B Metazoa - 241%3B Fungi - 181%3B Plants - 121%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 494 (source: NCBI BLink).;conf_rating=*****;Dbxref=PMID:16055634,gene:2075729,UniProt:Q8VYG2
