Chr3	Araport11	gene	3379168	3381621	.	+	.	ID=AT3G10800;Name=AT3G10800;Note=Basic-leucine zipper (bZIP) transcription factor family protein;curator_summary=Encodes bZIP28%2C a putative membrane-tethered transcriptional factor. Up-regulated in response to heat%3B a bZIP28 null mutant has a heat-sensitive phenotype.  bZIP28 has a similar domain structure to the mammalian ATF6 protein involved in the unfolded protein response (UPR)%2C and shares a bZIP domain%2C transmembrane domain%2C and a canonical S1P cleavage site. The bZIP28 seems to be glycosylated in vivo. bZIP28 does not appear to be transcriptionally up-regulated by UPR-inducing tunicamycin (TM) treatment. But%2C the expression level of three UPR-related genes is reduced in TM-treated zip28 mutants relative to wild type seedlings. And several UPR genes are transcriptionally upregulated when an N-terminal portion of the bZIP28 protein is expressed using the 35S promoter. A myc:bZIP28 fusion protein appears to be cleaved%2C likely at a canonical S2 cleavage site%2C following a TM treatment or a DTT stress-inducing treatment%2C but not a salt treatment. A portion of the  mGFP:bZIP28 protein present in root cells appears to translocate from the cytoplasm and ER to the nucleus following TM treatment.;symbol=BZIP28;computational_description=BZIP28%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Basic-leucine zipper (bZIP) transcription factor (InterPro:IPR004827)%2C bZIP transcription factor%2C bZIP-1 (InterPro:IPR011616)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Basic-leucine zipper (bZIP) transcription factor family protein (TAIR:AT2G40950.1)%3B Has 1906 Blast hits to 1391 proteins in 215 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 248%3B Metazoa - 700%3B Fungi - 222%3B Plants - 463%3B Viruses - 4%3B Other Eukaryotes - 269 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:11118137,PMID:11906833,PMID:14756312,PMID:15226410,PMID:16731568,PMID:17577400,PMID:17662035,PMID:18156219,PMID:18650403,PMID:18634751,PMID:18775970,PMID:18849477,PMID:20207753,PMID: