Chr3	Araport11	gene	3729305	3731251	.	-	.	ID=AT3G11820;Name=AT3G11820;Note=syntaxin of plants 121;curator_summary=Encodes a syntaxin localized at the plasma membrane (SYR1%2C Syntaxin Related Protein 1%2C also known as SYP121%2C PENETRATION1/PEN1).  SYR1/PEN1 is a member of the SNARE superfamily proteins.  SNARE proteins are involved in cell signaling%2C vesicle traffic%2C growth and development.  SYR1/PEN1 functions in positioning anchoring of the KAT1 K+ channel protein at the plasma membrane. Transcription is upregulated by abscisic acid%2C suggesting a role in ABA signaling.  Also functions in non-host resistance against barley powdery mildew%2C Blumeria graminis sp. hordei.  SYR1/PEN1 is a nonessential component of the preinvasive resistance against Colletotrichum fungus. Required for mlo resistance. The syp121 point mutation results in stomatal phenotypes that reduce CO2 assimilation%2C slow vegetative growth and increase water use efficiency in the whole plant%2C conditional upon high light intensities and low relative humidity.;symbol=SYP121;Alias=AT-SYR1,ATSYP121,ATSYR1,SYNTAXIN RELATED PROTEIN 1,PEN1,PENETRATION1,SYR1,SYNTAXIN RELATED PROTEIN 1;full_name=syntaxin of plants 121;computational_description=syntaxin of plants 121 (SYP121)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: protein anchor%2C SNAP receptor activity%3B INVOLVED IN: in 13 processes%3B LOCATED IN: SNARE complex%2C plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 24 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Target SNARE coiled-coil domain (InterPro:IPR000727)%2C Syntaxin/epimorphin%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR006012)%2C t-SNARE (InterPro:IPR010989)%2C Syntaxin%2C N-terminal (InterPro:IPR006011)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: syntaxin of plants 124 (TAIR:AT1G61290.1)%3B Has 2385 Blast hits to 2376 proteins in 301 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 6%3B Metazoa - 1106%3B Fungi - 480%3B Plants - 466%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 327 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:11