Chr3	Araport11	gene	3934000	3936758	.	+	.	ID=AT3G12360;Name=AT3G12360;Note=Ankyrin repeat family protein;curator_summary=Encodes a protein with an ankyrin motif and transmembrane domains that is involved in salt tolerance. Expressed throughout the plant and localized to the plasma membrane. Loss of function mutations show an increased tolerance to salt based on assaying seedling growth in the presence of salt. In the mutants%2C induction of genes required for production of reactive oxygen species is reduced suggesting that itn1 promotes ROS production.  It interacts with RCN1 in vivo and may regulate its subcellular localization.;symbol=ITN1;full_name=INCREASED TOLERANCE TO NACL;computational_description=INCREASED TOLERANCE TO NACL (ITN1)%3B INVOLVED IN: response to salt stress%3B LOCATED IN: plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 24 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Ankyrin repeat-containing domain (InterPro:IPR020683)%2C Ankyrin repeat (InterPro:IPR002110)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Ankyrin repeat family protein (TAIR:AT3G09550.1)%3B Has 61607 Blast hits to 26705 proteins in 1191 species: Archae - 49%3B Bacteria - 5778%3B Metazoa - 28187%3B Fungi - 6605%3B Plants - 4929%3B Viruses - 594%3B Other Eukaryotes - 15465 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:18650403,PMID:18643991,PMID:22664102,locus:2092522;locus_type=protein_coding
