Chr3	Araport11	gene	4146399	4154895	.	+	.	ID=AT3G12980;Name=AT3G12980;Note=histone acetyltransferase of the CBP family 5;curator_summary=Encodes an enzyme with histone acetyltransferase activity that can use both H3 and H4 histones as substrates.  No  single prior lysine acetylation is sufficient to block HAC5 acetylation of the H3 or H4 peptides%2C  suggesting that HAC5 can acetylate any  of several lysines present in the peptides. Di-acetylation of  both lysines 9 and 14 on the H3 peptide significantly reduces  the level of incorporated radioactive acetylation catalyzed by  HAC5%2C indicating that HAC5 may acetylate either lysine 9 or  lysine 14.;symbol=HAC5;Alias=ATHPCAT4,HISTONE ACETYLTRANSFERASE OF THE CBP FAMILY 5;full_name=histone acetyltransferase of the CBP family 5;computational_description=histone acetyltransferase of the CBP family 5 (HAC5)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: histone acetyltransferase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: flower development%2C protein amino acid acetylation%3B LOCATED IN: nucleus%3B EXPRESSED IN: 26 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 15 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Histone H3-K56 acetyltransferase%2C RTT109 (InterPro:IPR013178)%2C Zinc finger%2C PHD-type%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR019786)%2C Zinc finger%2C TAZ-type (InterPro:IPR000197)%2C Zinc finger%2C PHD-type (InterPro:IPR001965)%2C Zinc finger%2C FYVE/PHD-type (InterPro:IPR011011)%2C Zinc finger%2C ZZ-type (InterPro:IPR000433)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: histone acetyltransferase of the CBP family 1 (TAIR:AT1G79000.1)%3B Has 1382 Blast hits to 1050 proteins in 154 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 14%3B Metazoa - 567%3B Fungi - 56%3B Plants - 349%3B Viruses - 4%3B Other Eukaryotes - 392 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12466527,PMID:16214899,PMID:16489130,PMID:16720694,PMID:17144897,PMID:17877703,PMID:18775970,PMID:24614176,locus:2089285;locus_type=protein_coding
