Chr3	Araport11	gene	4231395	4234206	.	-	.	ID=AT3G13170;Name=AT3G13170;Note=Spo11/DNA topoisomerase VI%2C subunit A protein;curator_summary=Encodes AtSPO11-1%2C one of the three Arabidopsis homologues of the archaeal DNA topoisomerase VIA subunit (topo VIA).  Required for meiotic recombination.  AtSPO11-1 and AtSPO11-2 have overlapping functions (i.e. both required for meiotic recombination) whereas AtSPO11-3 functions in DNA replication. AtSPO11-1 accumulates in foci in early G2. At 1 h post-S phase%2C no foci are observed%2C but by  3 h a majority (80%25) of meiocytes at this time point  contain %3E50 foci. However%2C by 5 h%2C AtSPO11-1 foci are  no longer detectable. This suggests that the protein undergoes  a rapid cycle of accumulation and disappearance  in meiocytes over a period of between 1 and 5 h post-S  phase.;symbol=ATSPO11-1;computational_description=ATSPO11-1%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Spo11/DNA topoisomerase VI%2C subunit A%2C N-terminal (InterPro:IPR013049)%2C Meiotic recombination%2C Spo11 (InterPro:IPR013048)%2C Spo11/DNA topoisomerase VI%2C subunit A (InterPro:IPR002815)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Spo11/DNA topoisomerase VI%2C subunit A protein (TAIR:AT5G02820.1)%3B Has 908 Blast hits to 908 proteins in 313 species: Archae - 216%3B Bacteria - 16%3B Metazoa - 170%3B Fungi - 122%3B Plants - 151%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 233 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:11157765,PMID:17785529,PMID:17965269,PMID:18007598,PMID:19763177,PMID:20423461,PMID:20585549,PMID:22248237,PMID:22974522,PMID:24656236,locus:2090044;locus_type=protein_coding
