Chr3	Araport11	gene	4797828	4799612	.	-	.	ID=AT3G14370;Name=AT3G14370;Note=Protein kinase superfamily protein;curator_summary=The WAG2 and its homolog%2C WAG1 each encodes protein-serine/threonine kinase that are nearly 70%25 identical to PsPK3 protein. All three together with CsPK3 belong to PsPK3-type kinases. At the N-terminus%2C all four possess a serine/threonine-rich domain. They are closely related to Arabidopsis kinases PINOID. wag1/wag2 double mutants exhibit a pronounced wavy root phenotype when grown vertically on agar plates (while wild-type plants develop wavy roots only on plates inclined to angles less than 90 degrees)%2C indicating an overlapping role for WAG1 and WAG2 as suppressors of root waving. Simultaneous disruption of PID(AT2G34650) and its 3 closest homologs (PID2/AT2G26700%2C WAG1/AT1G53700%2C and WAG2/AT3G14370) abolishes the formation of cotyledons.;symbol=WAG2;computational_description=WAG2%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Protein kinase%2C catalytic domain (InterPro:IPR000719)%2C Serine/threonine-protein kinase domain (InterPro:IPR002290)%2C Serine/threonine-protein kinase-like domain (InterPro:IPR017442)%2C Protein kinase-like domain (InterPro:IPR011009)%2C Serine/threonine-protein kinase%2C active site (InterPro:IPR008271)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: WAG 1 (TAIR:AT1G53700.1)%3B Has 104032 Blast hits to 102948 proteins in 2832 species: Archae - 68%3B Bacteria - 12398%3B Metazoa - 38403%3B Fungi - 11620%3B Plants - 23519%3B Viruses - 432%3B Other Eukaryotes - 17592 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:13678909,PMID:15713015,PMID:16460509,PMID:16920880,PMID:19291320,PMID:20736450,PMID:20833732,PMID:20823065,PMID:25281709,locus:2091035;locus_type=protein_coding
