Chr3	Araport11	gene	5644593	5646557	.	+	.	ID=AT3G16570;Name=AT3G16570;Note=rapid alkalinization factor 23;curator_summary=Encodes RALF23%2C a member of a diversely expressed predicted peptide family showing sequence similarity to tobacco Rapid Alkalinization Factor (RALF)%2C and is believed to play an essential role in the physiology of Arabidopsis.  Consists of a single exon and is characterized by a conserved C-terminal motif and N-terminal signal peptide.  RALF23 is significantly downregulated by brassinolide treatment of seedlings.   Overexpression of AtRALF23 impairs brassinolide-induced hypocotyls elongation%2C and mature overexpressing plants are shorter and bushier. RALF23 overexpression produces slower growing seedlings with roots that have reduced capacity to acidify the rhizosphere.;symbol=RALF23;Alias=ATRALF23,ARABIDOPSIS RAPID ALKALINIZATION FACTOR 23;full_name=rapid alkalinization factor 23;computational_description=rapid alkalinization factor 23 (RALF23)%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Rapid ALkalinization Factor (InterPro:IPR008801)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: ralf-like 33 (TAIR:AT4G15800.1)%3B Has 261 Blast hits to 261 proteins in 20 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 2%3B Plants - 259%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 0 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12611624,locus:2089323;locus_type=protein_coding
