Chr3	Araport11	gene	5669317	5670842	.	-	.	ID=AT3G16640;Name=AT3G16640;Note=translationally controlled tumor protein;curator_summary=Encodes a protein homologous to  translationally controlled tumor protein (TCTP) from Drosophila. In flies%2C TCTP functions guanine nucleotide exchange factor in the TOR signaling pathway. TCTP is expressed throughout the plant with highest levels seen in meristematic regions of the shoot and root. Loss of function alleles are not transmitted through the male gametophyte due to defects in pollen tube growth. Hypomorphs%2C generated through RNAi%2C are dwarf and have smaller cells. These plants also have defects in lateral and primary root growth as well as root hair growth. The phenotypes are similar to TOR mutants suggesting that TCTP functions in the is pathway in Arabidopsis as well.;symbol=TCTP;Alias=AtTCTP2;full_name=translationally controlled tumor protein;computational_description=translationally controlled tumor protein (TCTP)%3B INVOLVED IN: in 8 processes%3B LOCATED IN: in 6 components%3B EXPRESSED IN: 28 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 17 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Translationally controlled tumour protein (InterPro:IPR018105)%2C Mss4/translationally controlled tumour-associated TCTP (InterPro:IPR011323)%2C Translationally controlled tumour protein%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR018103)%2C Mss4-like (InterPro:IPR011057)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Methionine sulfoxide reductase (MSS4-like) family protein (TAIR:AT3G05540.1)%3B Has 867 Blast hits to 867 proteins in 310 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 452%3B Fungi - 160%3B Plants - 158%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 97 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:11826309,PMID:14617064,PMID:14595688,PMID:14730065,PMID:15489285,PMID:16247729,PMID:16236172,PMID:16502469,PMID:16902407,PMID:17028151,PMID:17259181,PMID:17672910,PMID:17828791,PMID:18218973,PMID:18210371,PMID:18315867,PMID:18441215,PMID:18650403,PMID:18775970,PMID