Chr3	Araport11	gene	6019973	6021147	.	-	.	ID=AT3G17600;Name=AT3G17600;Note=indole-3-acetic acid inducible 31;curator_summary=Encodes a member of the Aux/IAA family of proteins implicated in auxin signaling. IAA31 shares several residues with the conserved domain II region%2C believed to act as a degron in many of the rapidly degraded Aux/IAA family members. An IAA31 fusion protein is quite long-lived%2C but can be degraded more rapidly in the presence of auxin. Unlike many other family members%2C IAA31 transcript levels do not rise in response to auxin. Nevertheless%2C overexpression of IAA31 leads to defects in auxin-related processes such as  gravitropism%2C root development%2C shoot development%2C and cotyledon vascular development.;symbol=IAA31;full_name=indole-3-acetic acid inducible 31;computational_description=indole-3-acetic acid inducible 31 (IAA31)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: sequence-specific DNA binding transcription factor activity%3B INVOLVED IN: gravitropism%2C response to auxin stimulus%2C shoot system development%2C root development%3B LOCATED IN: nucleus%2C chloroplast%3B EXPRESSED IN: stem%2C rosette leaf%2C fruit%2C root%2C flower%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Aux/IAA-ARF-dimerisation (InterPro:IPR011525)%2C AUX/IAA protein (InterPro:IPR003311)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: indole-3-acetic acid inducible 30 (TAIR:AT3G62100.1)%3B Has 1954 Blast hits to 1953 proteins in 77 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 1953%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 1 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:11118137,PMID:12036262,PMID:14576160,PMID:15078335,PMID:15247399,PMID:16284307,PMID:16489122,PMID:16934950,PMID:17360592,PMID:18298415,PMID:23682113,PMID:23791732,locus:2090527;locus_type=protein_coding
