Chr3	Araport11	gene	6577724	6590253	.	+	.	ID=AT3G19050;Name=AT3G19050;Note=phragmoplast orienting kinesin 2;curator_summary=PHRAGMOPLAST ORIENTING KINESIN 2 is one of the two Arabidopsis homologs isolated in yeast two-hybrid screen for interaction partners of maize gene TANGLED1 (TAN1). Based on sequence homology in their motor domains%2C POK1 and POK2 belong to the kinesin-12 class which also includes the well-characterized group of phragmoplast-associated kinesins AtPAKRPs. Both kinesins are composed of an N-terminal motor domain throughout the entire C terminus and putative cargo binding tail domains. The expression domains for POK2 constructs were broader than those for POK1%3B both are expressed in tissues enriched for dividing cells. The phenotype of pok1/pok2 double mutants strongly resembles that of maize tan1 mutants%2C characterized by misoriented mitotic cytoskeletal arrays and misplaced cell walls.;symbol=POK2;full_name=phragmoplast orienting kinesin 2;computational_description=phragmoplast orienting kinesin 2 (POK2)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: microtubule motor activity%2C ATP binding%3B INVOLVED IN: cytokinesis%3B EXPRESSED IN: root vascular system%2C primary root tip%2C lateral root primordium%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Kinesin%2C motor region%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR019821)%2C Kinesin%2C motor domain (InterPro:IPR001752)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: phragmoplast orienting kinesin 1 (TAIR:AT3G17360.1)%3B Has 204267 Blast hits to 80386 proteins in 3219 species: Archae - 3327%3B Bacteria - 35963%3B Metazoa - 90351%3B Fungi - 17822%3B Plants - 12667%3B Viruses - 746%3B Other Eukaryotes - 43391 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:16530461,PMID:16682350,PMID:19011093,PMID:21284606,locus:2085844;locus_type=protein_coding
