Chr3	Araport11	gene	7912905	7919707	.	+	.	ID=AT3G22380;Name=AT3G22380;Note=time for coffee;curator_summary=Encodes a nucleus-acting plant-specific clock regulator working close to the central oscillator and affecting the circadian gating of light responses.  Circadian gating is the alteration of circadian phase according to the photoperiod of the entraining day/light cycle and the rhythmic antagonism of light responses in the early subjective night.  TIC differentially regulates CCA1 and PRR9 from LHY%2C with LHY expression as a dominant genetic target of TIC action. Also shown to be invoved in the maintenance of Arabidopsis thaliana metabolic homeostasis.;symbol=TIC;full_name=TIME FOR COFFEE;computational_description=TIME FOR COFFEE (TIC)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: TIC-like (TAIR:AT3G63180.1)%3B Has 35078 Blast hits to 21616 proteins in 942 species: Archae - 10%3B Bacteria - 2414%3B Metazoa - 18018%3B Fungi - 6283%3B Plants - 1621%3B Viruses - 189%3B Other Eukaryotes - 6543 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:14555691,PMID:17496120,PMID:18775970,PMID:19828447,PMID:19847819,PMID:22693280,PMID:23204504,PMID:23372012,PMID:23869666,PMID:23845039,PMID:24277277,PMID:24974385,locus:2087812;locus_type=protein_coding
