Chr3	Araport11	mRNA	8567572	8574209	.	-	.	ID=AT3G23780.2;Parent=AT3G23780;Name=AT3G23780.2;Note=nuclear RNA polymerase D2A;curator_summary=This gene encodes the second largest%2C catalytic subunit of the nuclear DNA-dependent RNA polymerase IV (aka RNA polymerase D). The NRPD2 protein is found at nuclear foci that overlap or are adjacent to chromocentromeres but are not fully coincident with chromocentromeres. The loss of NRPD2 leads to the loss of cytosine methylation at pericentromeric 5S genes and AtSN1 retroelements but has no discernible effect on centromere repeat methylation. This suggests that Pol IV primarily affects facultative heterochromatin rather than constitutive heterochromatin.;conf_class=4;symbol=NRPD2A;Alias=DMS2,DEFECTIVE IN MERISTEM SILENCING 2,DRD2,NRPD2,NRPE2,OCP1,OVEREXPRESSOR OF CATIONIC PEROXIDASE 1;full_name=nuclear RNA polymerase D2A;computational_description=nuclear RNA polymerase D2A (NRPD2A)%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: DNA-directed RNA polymerase%2C subunit 2%2C domain 6 (InterPro:IPR007120)%2C RNA polymerase Rpb2%2C domain 7 (InterPro:IPR007641)%2C RNA polymerase%2C beta subunit%2C protrusion (InterPro:IPR007644)%2C RNA polymerase Rpb2%2C domain 3 (InterPro:IPR007645)%2C DNA-directed RNA polymerase%2C subunit 2 (InterPro:IPR015712)%2C RNA polymerase Rpb2%2C domain 2 (InterPro:IPR007642)%2C RNA polymerase Rpb2%2C domain 4 (InterPro:IPR007646)%2C RNA polymerase%2C beta subunit%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR007121)%2C RNA polymerase Rpb2%2C domain 5 (InterPro:IPR007647)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: nuclear RNA polymerase D2B (TAIR:AT3G18090.1).;conf_rating=***;Dbxref=gene:6530297101,UniProt:Q9LK40
