Chr3	Araport11	gene	9132068	9134099	.	+	.	ID=AT3G25070;Name=AT3G25070;Note=RPM1 interacting protein 4;curator_summary=Encodes a member of the R protein complex and may represent a virulence target of type III pili effector proteins (virulence factors) from bacterial pathogens%2C which is 'guarded' by R protein complex (RPM1 and RPS2 proteins). RIN4 physically interacts with RPS2 and RPM1 in vivo. Bacterial avirulence (Avr) effectors AvrB%2C AvrRpm1%2C and AvrRpt2 induce a mobility shift in RIN4 and expression of AvrRpt2 induces rapid degradation of RIN4. RIN4 contains 2 sites for AvrRpt2 autocleavage%2C called RCS1 and RCS2. Overexpression of RIN4 inhibits multiple phenotypes associated with AvrRpt2 function and also inhibits PAMP-induced defense signaling. Attached to the plasma membrane at its carboxyl terminus. Cleaved  by AvrRpt2 at two PxFGxW motifs%2C one releasing a large portion of RIN4 from the  plasma membrane and both exposing amino-terminal residues that destabilized the carboxyl-terminal cleavage products by targeting them for N-end ubiquitylation and proteasomal degradation. Major virulence target of the TTSE HopF2Pto.;symbol=RIN4;Alias=AtRIN4;full_name=RPM1 interacting protein 4;computational_description=RPM1 interacting protein 4 (RIN4)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: protein binding%3B INVOLVED IN: in 6 processes%3B LOCATED IN: plasma membrane%2C membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 22 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: RPM1-interacting protein 4%2C defence response (InterPro:IPR008700)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: defense protein-related (TAIR:AT5G48657.2)%3B Has 373 Blast hits to 371 proteins in 56 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 8%3B Metazoa - 13%3B Fungi - 2%3B Plants - 331%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 19 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:11607554,PMID:11955429,PMID:12581527,PMID:12581526,PMID:12620215,PMID:12950919,PMID:15000398,PMID:15361584,PMID:15684089,PMID:15546361,PMID:15746386,PMID:157