Chr3	Araport11	gene	11960298	11961917	.	-	.	ID=AT3G30350;Name=AT3G30350;Note=root meristem growth factor-like protein;curator_summary=Encodes a root meristem growth factor (RGF).  Belongs to a family of functionally redundant homologous peptides that are secreted%2C tyrosine-sulfated%2C and expressed mainly in the stem cell area and the innermost layer of central columella cells. RGFs are required for maintenance of the root stem cell niche and transit amplifying cell proliferation.  Members of this family include: At5g60810 (RGF1)%2C At1g13620 (RGF2)%2C At2g04025 (RGF3)%2C At3g30350 (RGF4)%2C At5g51451 (RGF5)%2C At4g16515 (RGF6)%2C At3g02240 (RGF7)%2C At2g03830 (RGF8) and At5g64770 (RGF9).;symbol=RGF4;Alias=GLV3,GOLVEN 3;full_name=root meristem growth factor 4;computational_description=root meristem growth factor 4 (RGF4)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: molecular_function unknown%3B INVOLVED IN: biological_process unknown%3B LOCATED IN: endomembrane system%3B EXPRESSED IN: hypocotyl%2C root%3B Has 4 Blast hits to 4 proteins in 2 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 4%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 0 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:20798316,PMID:22421050,locus:2102891;locus_type=protein_coding
