Chr3	Araport11	gene	14320943	14324069	.	+	.	ID=AT3G42170;Name=AT3G42170;Note=BED zinc finger and hAT dimerization domain-containing protein DAYSLEEPER;curator_summary=transposase-like gene with conserved domains from the family of hAT transposases that includes hobo from Drosophila melanogaster%2C Activator (Ac) from maize%2C and Tam3 from snapdragon but lacks several amino acids known to be essential for Ac transposition5. The DAYSLEEPER gene lacks 8 bp duplications and TIRs (a common feature of transcriptionally silent hAT transposases)%2C however%2C DAYSLEEPER expression was detected%2C and several expressed sequence tags are available. The expression seems to be under the control of factors determining the circadian rhythm. DAYSLEEPER was isolated as a factor binding to a motif (Kubox1) present in the upstream region of the Arabidopsis DNA repair gene Ku70. Mutant plants lacking DAYSLEEPER or strongly overexpressing this gene do not develop in a normal manner.;symbol=DAYSLEEPER;full_name=DAYSLEEPER;computational_description=BED zinc finger %3BhAT family dimerisation domain%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: HAT dimerisation (InterPro:IPR008906)%2C Zinc finger%2C BED-type predicted (InterPro:IPR003656)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: BED zinc finger %3BhAT family dimerisation domain (TAIR:AT1G18560.1)%3B Has 1233 Blast hits to 1128 proteins in 97 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 4%3B Metazoa - 232%3B Fungi - 219%3B Plants - 755%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 23 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:16015335,PMID:16461884,PMID:16776291,PMID:18650403,PMID:23067104,PMID:24330683,locus:2100809;locus_type=protein_coding
