Chr3	Araport11	gene	15986624	15989505	.	+	.	ID=AT3G44310;Name=AT3G44310;Note=nitrilase 1;curator_summary=Mutants are resistant to indole-3-acetonitrile (IAN). NIT1 catalyzes the terminal activation step in indole-acetic acid biosynthesis. Predominantly expressed isoform of nitrilase isoenzyme family.   Aggregation of NIT1 in cells directly abutting wound sites is one of the earliest events associated with wound and herbicide-induced cell death.  The protein undergoes thiolation following treatment with the  oxidant tert-butylhydroperoxide. It is also involved in the conversion of IAN to IAM (indole-3-acetamide) and other non-auxin-related metabolic processes.;symbol=NIT1;Alias=ATNIT1,A. THALIANA NITRILASE 1,NITI;full_name=nitrilase 1;computational_description=nitrilase 1 (NIT1)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: indole-3-acetonitrile nitrilase activity%2C nitrilase activity%2C indole-3-acetonitrile nitrile hydratase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: indoleacetic acid biosynthetic process%3B LOCATED IN: apoplast%2C chloroplast%2C plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: guard cell%2C cultured cell%2C leaf%3B EXPRESSED DURING: seedling growth%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Nitrilase/cyanide hydratase and apolipoprotein N-acyltransferase (InterPro:IPR003010)%2C Nitrilase/cyanide hydratase%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR000132)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: nitrilase 2 (TAIR:AT3G44300.1)%3B Has 7572 Blast hits to 7496 proteins in 1731 species: Archae - 139%3B Bacteria - 4902%3B Metazoa - 443%3B Fungi - 562%3B Plants - 319%3B Viruses - 11%3B Other Eukaryotes - 1196 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:8022831,PMID:12430025,PMID:16055689,PMID:20507526,PMID:22007024,PMID:23289948,locus:2095690;locus_type=protein_coding
