Chr3	Araport11	gene	16617398	16621370	.	+	.	ID=AT3G45290;Name=AT3G45290;Note=Seven transmembrane MLO family protein;curator_summary=A member of a large family of seven-transmembrane domain proteins specific to plants%2C homologs of the barley mildew resistance locus o (MLO) protein. The Arabidopsis genome contains 15 genes encoding MLO proteins%2C with localization in plasma membrane. Phylogenetic analysis revealed four clades of closely-related AtMLO genes. ATMLO3 belongs to the clade IV%2C with AtMLO2%2C AtMLO6 and AtMLO12. The gene is expressed during early seedling growth%2C in primary root and lateral root primordia%2C in fruit abscission zone%2C in vascular system of cotyledons and in trichomes of young leaves%2C%3B it was not expressed in mature rosette leaves%2C as shown by GUS activity patterns. The expression of several phylogenetically closely-related AtMLO genes showed similar or overlapping tissue specificity and analogous responsiveness to external stimuli%2C suggesting functional redundancy%2C co-function%2C or antagonistic function(s).;symbol=MLO3;Alias=ATMLO3,MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 3;full_name=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 3;computational_description=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 3 (MLO3)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: calmodulin binding%3B INVOLVED IN: cell death%2C defense response%3B LOCATED IN: integral to membrane%2C plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 29 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 14 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Mlo-related protein (InterPro:IPR004326)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Seven transmembrane MLO family protein (TAIR:AT2G39200.1)%3B Has 534 Blast hits to 527 proteins in 60 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 10%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 520%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 4 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12569425,PMID:15990873,PMID:16525893,PMID:18805951,locus:2078292;locus_type=protein_coding
