Chr3	Araport11	gene	17183042	17186959	.	+	.	ID=AT3G46640;Name=AT3G46640;Note=Homeodomain-like superfamily protein;curator_summary=Encodes a myb family transcription factor with a single Myb DNA-binding domain (type SHAQKYF) that is unique to plants and is essential for circadian rhythms%2C specifically for transcriptional regulation within the circadian clock.   LUX is required for normal rhythmic expression of multiple clock outputs in both constant light and darkness.  It is coregulated with TOC1 and seems to be repressed by CCA1 and LHY by direct binding of these proteins to the evening element in the LUX promoter.;symbol=PCL1;Alias=LUX,LUX ARRHYTHMO;full_name=PHYTOCLOCK 1;computational_description=PHYTOCLOCK 1 (PCL1)%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Homeodomain-like (InterPro:IPR009057)%2C Myb%2C DNA-binding (InterPro:IPR014778)%2C Myb-like DNA-binding domain%2C SHAQKYF class (InterPro:IPR006447)%2C HTH transcriptional regulator%2C Myb-type%2C DNA-binding (InterPro:IPR017930)%2C Homeodomain-related (InterPro:IPR012287)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Homeodomain-like superfamily protein (TAIR:AT5G59570.1)%3B Has 1709 Blast hits to 1707 proteins in 80 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 29%3B Metazoa - 20%3B Fungi - 11%3B Plants - 1622%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 27 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:11118137,PMID:16006522,PMID:16164597,PMID:17132630,PMID:21236673,PMID:21447790,PMID:21753751,PMID:22327739,PMID:22311777,PMID:22307044,PMID:23558642,PMID:23731278,PMID:24443443,PMID:24377444,PMID:24500967,PMID:24706549,PMID:24690904,PMID:24974385,PMID:25147271,PMID:25332490,PMID:25557667,locus:2075200;locus_type=protein_coding
