Chr3	Araport11	gene	18071454	18074641	.	+	.	ID=AT3G48750;Name=AT3G48750;Note=cell division control 2;curator_summary=A-type cyclin-dependent kinase. Together with its specific inhibitor%2C  the Kip-related protein%2C KRP2 they regulate the mitosis-to-endocycle transition during  leaf development. Dominant negative mutations abolish cell division. Loss of function phenotype has reduced fertility with failure to transmit via pollen. Pollen development is arrested at the  second mitotic division. Expression is regulated by environmental and chemical signals. Part of the promoter is responsible for expression in trichomes. Functions as a positive regulator of cell proliferation during development of the male gametophyte%2C embryo and endosperm. Phosphorylation of threonine 161 is required for activation of its associated kinase.;symbol=CDC2;Alias=CDC2A,CDC2AAT,CDK2,CDKA1,CDKA%3B1;full_name=cell division control 2;computational_description=cell division control 2 (CDC2)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: protein binding%2C protein kinase activity%2C cyclin-dependent protein kinase activity%2C kinase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: in 8 processes%3B LOCATED IN: in 6 components%3B EXPRESSED IN: 23 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Protein kinase%2C ATP binding site (InterPro:IPR017441)%2C Protein kinase%2C catalytic domain (InterPro:IPR000719)%2C Serine/threonine-protein kinase domain (InterPro:IPR002290)%2C Serine/threonine-protein kinase-like domain (InterPro:IPR017442)%2C Protein kinase-like domain (InterPro:IPR011009)%2C Serine/threonine-protein kinase%2C active site (InterPro:IPR008271)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: cyclin-dependent kinase B1%3B2 (TAIR:AT2G38620.2)%3B Has 126125 Blast hits to 124135 proteins in 4221 species: Archae - 112%3B Bacteria - 14002%3B Metazoa - 46757%3B Fungi - 13170%3B Plants - 30525%3B Viruses - 484%3B Other Eukaryotes - 21075 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:8570631,PMID:1937013,PMID:11442060,PM