Chr3	Araport11	gene	18417568	18421263	.	+	.	ID=AT3G49670;Name=AT3G49670;Note=Leucine-rich receptor-like protein kinase family protein;curator_summary=Encodes a CLAVATA1-related receptor kinase-like protein required for both shoot and flower meristem function.  Very similar to BAM1%2Cwith more than 85%25 a.a. identity. It has a broad expression pattern and is involved in vascular strand development in the leaf%2C control of leaf shape%2C size and symmetry%2C male gametophyte development and ovule specification and function. Anthers of double mutants (bam1bam2) appeared abnormal at a very early stage and lack the endothecium%2C middle%2C and tapetum layers. Further analyses revealed that cells interior to the epidermis (in anther tissue) acquire some characteristics of pollen mother cells (PMCs)%2C suggesting defects in cell fate specification. The pollen mother-like cells degenerate before the completion of meiosis%2C suggesting that these cells are defective. In addition%2C the BAM2 expression pattern supports both an early role in promoting somatic cell fates and a subsequent function in the PMCs.;symbol=BAM2;full_name=BARELY ANY MERISTEM 2;computational_description=BARELY ANY MERISTEM 2 (BAM2)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: protein serine/threonine kinase activity%2C protein kinase activity%2C ATP binding%3B INVOLVED IN: in 9 processes%3B LOCATED IN: plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 29 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 15 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Protein kinase%2C catalytic domain (InterPro:IPR000719)%2C Leucine-rich repeat-containing N-terminal domain%2C type 2 (InterPro:IPR013210)%2C Leucine-rich repeat (InterPro:IPR001611)%2C Serine-threonine/tyrosine-protein kinase (InterPro:IPR001245)%2C Protein kinase-like domain (InterPro:IPR011009)%2C Serine/threonine-protein kinase%2C active site (InterPro:IPR008271)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Leucine-rich receptor-like protein kinase family protein (TAIR:AT5G65700.2)%3B Has 214102 Blast hits to 137812 proteins in 4967 species: Archae - 148%3B Bacteria - 22093%3B Metazoa - 65883%3B Fungi - 10747%3B Plants - 88678%3B Viruses - 437%3B Other Eukaryotes - 26116 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12972053,PMID:15086800,PMID:15509765,PMID:15695462,PMID:16367950,PMID:16751349,PMID:17217541,PMID:18650403,PMID:18780746,PMID:20179141,PMID:20626648,PMID:21051944,PMID:21477822,PMID:21750229,PMID:25626615,locus:2097310;locus_type=protein_coding
Chr3	Araport11	mRNA	18417568	18421263	.	+	.	ID=AT3G49670.1;Parent=AT3G49670;Name=AT3G49670.1;Note=Leucine-rich receptor-like protein kinase family protein;curator_summary=Encodes a CLAVATA1-related receptor kinase-like protein required for both shoot and flower meristem function.  Very similar to BAM1%2Cwith more than 85%25 a.a. identity. It has a broad expression pattern and is involved in vascular strand development in the leaf%2C control of leaf shape%2C size and symmetry%2C male gametophyte development and ovule specification and function. Anthers of double mutants (bam1bam2) appeared abnormal at a very early stage and lack the endothecium%2C middle%2C and tapetum layers. Further analyses revealed that cells interior to the epidermis (in anther tissue) acquire some characteristics of pollen mother cells (PMCs)%2C suggesting defects in cell fate specification. The pollen mother-like cells degenerate before the completion of meiosis%2C suggesting that these cells are defective. In addition%2C the BAM2 expression pattern supports both an early role in promoting somatic cell fates and a subsequent function in the PMCs.;conf_class=2;symbol=BAM2;full_name=BARELY ANY MERISTEM 2;computational_description=BARELY ANY MERISTEM 2 (BAM2)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: protein serine/threonine kinase activity%2C protein kinase activity%2C ATP binding%3B INVOLVED IN: in 9 processes%3B LOCATED IN: plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 29 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 15 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Protein kinase%2C catalytic domain (InterPro:IPR000719)%2C Leucine-rich repeat-containing N-terminal domain%2C type 2 (InterPro:IPR013210)%2C Leucine-rich repeat (InterPro:IPR001611)%2C Serine-threonine/tyrosine-protein kinase (InterPro:IPR001245)%2C Protein kinase-like domain (InterPro:IPR011009)%2C Serine/threonine-protein kinase%2C active site (InterPro:IPR008271)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Leucine-rich receptor-like protein kinase family protein (TAIR:AT5