Chr3	Araport11	gene	18800306	18801595	.	+	.	ID=AT3G50630;Name=AT3G50630;Note=KIP-related protein 2;curator_summary=Kip-related protein (KRP) gene%2C encodes CDK (cyclin-dependent kinase) inhibitor (CKI)%2C negative regulator of cell division. A member of seven KRP genes found in Arabidopsis thaliana. Differential expression patterns for distinct KRPs were revealed by in situ hybridization.  Gene was isolated from a yeast two hybrid screen as an interacting protein of CDC2A. Recombinant protein has a strong kinase inhibitor activity in vitro. Transcript is expressed in all tissues examined but is differentially distributed from ICK1. Controls the onset of the endoreduplication cycle through inhibition of CDKA%3B1. The KRP2 protein abundance is regulated by proteolysis through CDKB1%3B1 phosphorylation.;symbol=KRP2;Alias=ICK2;full_name=KIP-related protein 2;computational_description=KIP-related protein 2 (KRP2)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: protein binding%2C kinase inhibitor activity%2C cyclin-dependent protein kinase inhibitor activity%3B INVOLVED IN: negative regulation of cyclin-dependent protein kinase activity%2C DNA endoreduplication%3B LOCATED IN: nucleus%3B EXPRESSED IN: 24 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 9 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor (InterPro:IPR003175)%2C Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor%2C plant (InterPro:IPR016701)%3B Has 103 Blast hits to 103 proteins in 17 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 2%3B Fungi - 2%3B Plants - 97%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 2 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:16376885,PMID:19000158,PMID:19576768,PMID:20706207,PMID:21221633,PMID:21270057,PMID:21357490,PMID:22476290,PMID:23574394,PMID:23647236,PMID:24497510,PMID:24068796,PMID:24305734,locus:2101679;locus_type=protein_coding
