Chr3	Araport11	gene	18813949	18817405	.	-	.	ID=AT3G50660;Name=AT3G50660;Note=Cytochrome P450 superfamily protein;curator_summary=Encodes a 22%26#945%3B hydroxylase whose reaction is a rate-limiting step in brassinosteroid biosynthetic pathway. The protein is a member of CYP90B gene family. CLM is an epi-allele  with small%2C compressed rosette%2C reduced internode length%2C and reduced fertility%2C appears in selfed ddm mutant plants possibly due to loss of cytosine methylation. Transcripts accumulate in actively growing tissues%2C and GUS expression is negatively  regulated by brassinosteroids. Localized in the endoplasmic reticulum. The in vitro expressed protein can perform the C-22 hydroxylation of a variety of C27-%2C C28- and C29-sterols. Cholesterol was the best substrate%2C followed by campesterol. Sitosterol was a poor substrate.;symbol=DWF4;Alias=AtDWF4,CLM,CLOMAZONE-RESISTANT,CYP90B1,CYTOCHROME P450 90B1,PSC1,PARTIALLY SUPPRESSING  COI1 INSENSITIVITY TO JA 1,SAV1,SHADE AVOIDANCE 1,SNP2,SUPPRESSOR OF NPH4 2;full_name=DWARF 4;computational_description=DWARF 4 (DWF4)%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Cytochrome P450 (InterPro:IPR001128)%2C Cytochrome P450%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR017972)%2C Cytochrome P450%2C E-class%2C group I (InterPro:IPR002401)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Cytochrome P450 superfamily protein (TAIR:AT5G05690.1)%3B Has 31120 Blast hits to 31036 proteins in 1650 species: Archae - 61%3B Bacteria - 5303%3B Metazoa - 10591%3B Fungi - 5722%3B Plants - 7996%3B Viruses - 3%3B Other Eukaryotes - 1444 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:10069828,PMID:9490746,PMID:9490745,PMID:8901594,PMID:11319239,PMID:11489171,PMID:11346800,PMID:12114578,PMID:12226529,PMID:12350224,PMID:12529536,PMID:14676973,PMID:15908602,PMID:16407451,PMID:16460510,PMID:16632588,PMID:16906434,PMID:16960392,PMID:17668219,PMID:18650403,PMID:17908154,PMID:18394996,PMID:18175930,PMID:19741050,PMID:20009521,PMID:20169349,PMID:20435901,PMID:20685730,PMID:21284753,PM