Chr3	Araport11	gene	19135619	19136675	.	-	.	ID=AT3G51590;Name=AT3G51590;Note=lipid transfer protein 12;curator_summary=Encodes a member of the lipid transfer protein family.  Proteins of this family are generally small (~9 kD)%2C basic%2C expressed abundantly and contain eight Cys residues.  The proteins can bind fatty acids and acylCoA esters and can transfer several different phospholipids.  They are localized to the cell wall.  The LTP12 promoter is active exclusively in the tapetum during the uninucleate microspore and bicellular pollen stages. Predicted to be a member of PR-14 pathogenesis-related protein family with the following members:   At2g38540/LTP1%2C At2g38530/LTP2%2C At5g59320/LTP3%2C At5g59310/LTP4%2C At3g51600/LTP5%2C At3g08770/LTP6%2C At2g15050/LTP7%2C At2g18370/LTP8%2C At2g15325/LTP9%2C At5g01870/LTP10%2C At4g33355/LTP11%2C At3g51590/LTP12%2C At5g44265/LTP13%2C At5g62065/LTP14%2C At4g08530/LTP15.;symbol=LTP12;full_name=lipid transfer protein 12;computational_description=lipid transfer protein 12 (LTP12)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: lipid binding%3B INVOLVED IN: lipid transport%3B LOCATED IN: plant-type cell wall%3B EXPRESSED IN: 8 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: D pollen mother cell meiosis stage%2C 4 anthesis%2C petal differentiation and expansion stage%2C E expanded cotyledon stage%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Bifunctional inhibitor/plant lipid transfer protein/seed storage (InterPro:IPR016140)%2C Plant lipid transfer protein/seed storage/trypsin-alpha amylase inhibitor (InterPro:IPR003612)%2C Plant lipid transfer protein/Par allergen (InterPro:IPR000528)%2C Plant lipid transfer protein/hydrophobic protein%2C helical domain (InterPro:IPR013770)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: lipid transfer protein 3 (TAIR:AT5G59320.1)%3B Has 1073 Blast hits to 1072 proteins in 125 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 2%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 1069%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 2 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:10940464,PMID:1468