Chr3	Araport11	gene	19246936	19249200	.	-	.	ID=AT3G51880;Name=AT3G51880;Note=high mobility group B1;curator_summary=Encodes a protein belonging to the subgroup of HMGB (high mobility group B) proteins that have a distinctive DNA-binding motif%2C the HMG-box domain.  The motif confers non-sequence specific interaction with linear DNA and structure-specific binding to distorted DNA sites.  The HMGB proteins are involved in the assembly of nucleoprotein complexes. Can be phosphorylated by CK2alpha. In interphase cells%2C HMGB1 is found throughout the nucleus%2C whereas in mitotic cells it is not chromatin-associated.;symbol=HMGB1;Alias=AtHMGB1,NFD1,NUCLEOSOME/CHROMATIN ASSEMBLY FACTOR D1;full_name=high mobility group B1;computational_description=high mobility group B1 (HMGB1)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: chromatin binding%2C structural constituent of chromatin%2C DNA binding%2C sequence-specific DNA binding transcription factor activity%3B INVOLVED IN: chromatin assembly or disassembly%3B LOCATED IN: cytosol%2C chromatin%2C nuclear chromatin%2C nucleus%3B EXPRESSED IN: 26 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 15 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: High mobility group%2C superfamily (InterPro:IPR009071)%2C High mobility group%2C HMG1/HMG2 (InterPro:IPR000910)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: high mobility group B3 (TAIR:AT1G20696.3)%3B Has 22052 Blast hits to 13496 proteins in 725 species: Archae - 26%3B Bacteria - 633%3B Metazoa - 9857%3B Fungi - 2534%3B Plants - 1397%3B Viruses - 386%3B Other Eukaryotes - 7219 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:9461286,PMID:11118137,PMID:12653554,PMID:12837951,PMID:17114349,PMID:17827277,PMID:18650403,PMID:18822296,PMID:18775970,PMID:20123078,PMID:20940346,PMID:21348847,PMID:21543902,locus:2074368;locus_type=protein_coding
