Chr3	Araport11	gene	19267951	19269658	.	-	.	ID=AT3G51920;Name=AT3G51920;Note=calmodulin 9;curator_summary=encodes a divergent member of calmodulin%2C which is an EF-hand family of Ca2+-binding proteins. This gene is expressed in leaves%2C flowers and siliques. The gene functionally complements yeast calmodulin 1 (CAM1) but only  when selected against the plasmid harboring wild-type yeast sequences. Also the protein does not form formed a complex with a basic amphiphilic helical peptide in the presence of Ca2+ in vitro. Authors suggest that this gene may represent a Ca2+-binding sensor protein that interacts with a more limited set of target proteins than do more conventional CaM isoforms. Mutations in this gene alter plant responses to abiotic stress and abscisic acid.;symbol=CAM9;Alias=ATCML9,CML9,CALMODULIN LIKE PROTEIN 9;full_name=calmodulin 9;computational_description=calmodulin 9 (CAM9)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: calcium ion binding%3B INVOLVED IN: response to salt stress%2C response to water deprivation%2C detection of calcium ion%2C calcium-mediated signaling%2C response to abscisic acid stimulus%3B LOCATED IN: cytosol%2C nucleus%3B EXPRESSED IN: 24 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: EF-Hand 1%2C calcium-binding site (InterPro:IPR018247)%2C EF-HAND 2 (InterPro:IPR018249)%2C EF-hand-like domain (InterPro:IPR011992)%2C Calcium-binding EF-hand (InterPro:IPR002048)%2C EF-hand (InterPro:IPR018248)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: calmodulin 1 (TAIR:AT5G37780.1)%3B Has 22298 Blast hits to 16833 proteins in 1534 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 90%3B Metazoa - 8769%3B Fungi - 5904%3B Plants - 4665%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 2870 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:11855649,PMID:12372144,PMID:12609040,PMID:12753585,PMID:12045290,PMID:14557048,PMID:15047898,PMID:15276435,PMID:15347784,PMID:15720654,PMID:15713015,PMID:16023399,PMID:16214899,PMID:17227549,PMID:18650403,PMID:18643966,PMID:20627089,PMID:20736