Chr3	Araport11	gene	20045603	20048745	.	-	.	ID=AT3G54140;Name=AT3G54140;Note=peptide transporter 1;curator_summary=Encodes a di- and tri-peptide transporter that recognizes a variety of different amino acid combinations. GFP-tagged PTR1 localizes to the plasma membrane and has 8 to 11 predicted transmembrane domains. PTR1 is expressed in a number of different vascular tissues throughout the plant based on promoter:GUS expression analysis. ptr1 mutants have a lower dry weight than wild type plants when both are grown with Pro-Ala or Ala-Ala dipeptides as their nitrogen source%2C suggesting that PTR1 plays a role in dipeptide uptake in the roots. Furthermore N content of ptr1 mutants is lower than that of wild type plants when grown with Pro-Ala or a mixture of dipeptides as nitrogen source;symbol=PTR1;Alias=ATPTR1,ARABIDOPSIS THALIANA PEPTIDE TRANSPORTER 1,AtNPF8.1,NPF8.1,NRT1/ PTR family 8.1;full_name=peptide transporter 1;computational_description=peptide transporter 1 (PTR1)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: dipeptide transporter activity%2C tripeptide transporter activity%2C transporter activity%3B INVOLVED IN: dipeptide transport%2C oligopeptide transport%2C nitrogen compound metabolic process%2C tripeptide transport%3B LOCATED IN: plasma membrane%2C membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 40 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 10 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: PTR2 family proton/oligopeptide symporter%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR018456)%2C Oligopeptide transporter (InterPro:IPR000109)%2C Major facilitator superfamily%2C general substrate transporter (InterPro:IPR016196)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: peptide transporter  5 (TAIR:AT5G01180.1)%3B Has 8339 Blast hits to 7886 proteins in 1502 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 4164%3B Metazoa - 798%3B Fungi - 498%3B Plants - 2234%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 645 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:15500465,PMID:16581873,PMID:16684236,PMID:17481610,PMID:17586839,PMID:18753286,PMID:18780802,PMID:20501909,PMI