Chr3	Araport11	gene	20213406	20217653	.	+	.	ID=AT3G54610;Name=AT3G54610;Note=histone acetyltransferase of the GNAT family 1;curator_summary=Encodes a histone acetyltransferase that is plays a role in the determination of the embryonic root-shoot axis.  It is also required to regulate the floral meristem activity by modulating the extent of expression of WUS and AG.  In other eukaryotes%2C this protein is recruited to specific promoters by DNA binding transcription factors and is thought to promote transcription by acetylating the N-terminal tail of histone H3. The enzyme has indeed been shown to catalyse primarily the acetylation of H3 histone with only traces of H4 and H2A/B being acetylated. Non-acetylated H3 peptide or an H3 peptide that had been  previously acetylated on K9 both serve as excellent substrates  for HAG1-catalyzed acetylation. However%2C prior acetylation  of H3 lysine 14 blocks radioactive acetylation of the  peptide by HAG1.  HAG1 is specific for  histone H3 lysine 14.;symbol=HAG1;Alias=BGT,BIG TOP,GCN5,general control non-repressible 5,HAC3,HAG01,HAT1,HISTONE ACETYLTRANSFERASE 1;full_name=histone acetyltransferase of the GNAT family 1;computational_description=histone acetyltransferase of the GNAT family 1 (HAG1)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: histone acetyltransferase activity%2C DNA binding%2C H3 histone acetyltransferase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: flower development%2C histone acetylation%2C response to light stimulus%2C positive regulation of transcription%2C root morphogenesis%3B LOCATED IN: histone acetyltransferase complex%2C nucleus%3B EXPRESSED IN: 9 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 4 anthesis%2C petal differentiation and expansion stage%2C E expanded cotyledon stage%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: GCN5-related N-acetyltransferase%2C C-terminal (InterPro:IPR022610)%2C GCN5-related N-acetyltransferase (InterPro:IPR000182)%2C Bromodomain%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR018359)%2C Acyl-CoA N-acyltransferase (InterPro:IPR016181)%2C Bromodomain (InterPro:IPR001487)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: nuclear protein X1 (TAIR:AT5G63320.1)%3B Has 13698 Blast hits to 5805 proteins in 367 species: Archae - 4%3B Bacteria - 1437%3B Metazoa - 4852%3B Fungi - 1484%3B Plants - 516%3B Viruses - 1%3B Other Eukaryotes - 5404 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:10536141,PMID:7915839,PMID:11266554,PMID:12466527,PMID:12615937,PMID:12740375,PMID:16603259,PMID:16763149,PMID:17085686,PMID:17151888,PMID:17877703,PMID:18498779,PMID:18644002,PMID:19376933,PMID:19436261,PMID:19771450,PMID:19825652,PMID:20457643,PMID:20661629,locus:3354973;locus_type=protein_coding
