Chr3	Araport11	gene	20520930	20523098	.	-	.	ID=AT3G55360;Name=AT3G55360;Note=3-oxo-5-alpha-steroid 4-dehydrogenase family protein;curator_summary=Enoyl-CoA reductase is involved in all very long chain fatty acids (VLCFA) elongation reactions that are required for cuticular wax%2C storage lipid and sphingolipid metabolism. The protein is located in the ER%2C but in contrast to its yeast homolog TSC13 is not particularly enriched in the nuclear envelope-vacuole junction. Mutants in this gene show abnormal organ morphology and stem glossiness. Cells in all tissues are only about 1/3 of the size of wild type cells. The morphological changes are most likely to result from the reduction in the VLCFA content of sphingolipids. Mutants also show abnormalities in the endocytic membrane organization and transport.;symbol=CER10;Alias=ATTSC13,ECR,ENOYL-COA REDUCTASE,GLH6,GLASSY HAIR 6,TSC13;full_name=ECERIFERUM 10;computational_description=ECERIFERUM 10 (CER10)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: fatty acid elongase activity%2C trans-2-enoyl-CoA reductase (NADPH) activity%2C 3-oxo-5-alpha-steroid 4-dehydrogenase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: sphingolipid metabolic process%2C wax biosynthetic process%3B LOCATED IN: endoplasmic reticulum%2C fatty acid elongase complex%2C plasma membrane%2C endoplasmic reticulum membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 24 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: 3-oxo-5-alpha-steroid 4-dehydrogenase%2C C-terminal (InterPro:IPR001104)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: 3-oxo-5-alpha-steroid 4-dehydrogenase family protein (TAIR:AT5G16010.1)%3B Has 1087 Blast hits to 1087 proteins in 269 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 73%3B Metazoa - 353%3B Fungi - 144%3B Plants - 184%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 333 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:1847001,PMID:14673020,PMID:15829606,PMID:16618929,PMID:18650403,PMID:20145257,PMID:21617381,PMID:23505340,PMID:22268629,PMID:24319075,PMID:24014871,PMID:24692420,PMID:25305760,locus:2099911;lo