Chr3	Araport11	gene	21147558	21150238	.	+	.	ID=AT3G57130;Name=AT3G57130;Note=Ankyrin repeat family protein / BTB/POZ domain-containing protein;curator_summary=Encodes BOP1.  Contains Pfam domain%2C PF00023: Ankyrin repeat and Pfam domain%2C PF00651: BTB/POZ domain. Lines carrying recessive mutations exhibit a number of visible defects%2C most pronounced being ectopic outgrowths of in leaf petioles of rosette leaves. Along with BOP2%2C BOP1 is required for nectary development and  formation of normal abscission zones.Forms homodimers and heterodimers with BOP2. Nuclear localization is required for activity which includes positive regulation of AS2 in leaves. BOP1/2 promotes floral meristem fate and determinacy in a pathway targetting APETALA1 and AGAMOUS-LIKE24. PUCHI%2C BOP1 and BOP2 are redundantly required for expression of LFY and AP1. BOP1 is expressed in valve margin. Misexpression in stems causes short internodes and ectopic biosynthesis of lignin. BOP1 activity is antagonistic to BP (At4g08150) and PNY (At5g02030). BOP1 expression is restricted to pedicel axils by BP and PNY. BOP1 promotes KNAT6 (At1g23380) expression.;symbol=BOP1;full_name=BLADE ON PETIOLE 1;computational_description=BLADE ON PETIOLE 1 (BOP1)%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: BTB/POZ (InterPro:IPR013069)%2C BTB/POZ fold (InterPro:IPR011333)%2C Ankyrin repeat-containing domain (InterPro:IPR020683)%2C BTB/POZ-like (InterPro:IPR000210)%2C Ankyrin repeat (InterPro:IPR002110)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Ankyrin repeat family protein / BTB/POZ domain-containing protein (TAIR:AT2G41370.1)%3B Has 4143 Blast hits to 3880 proteins in 336 species: Archae - 25%3B Bacteria - 266%3B Metazoa - 1805%3B Fungi - 185%3B Plants - 1045%3B Viruses - 32%3B Other Eukaryotes - 785 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12441300,PMID:17601823,PMID:15564519,PMID:19482972,PMID:20118228,PMID:20626659,PMID:20610407,PMID:21235646,PMID:22114095,PMID:22751300,PMID:22992509,PMID:23116333,PMID:25371365,locus:208059